res/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":770.2533162434896,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":405.6666666666667,"r":527.6666666666666,"t":792.2533162434896},"charspan":[0,9],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/2","text":"MATERIALS"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"~2 56.5 Im and 26.3%, respectively, with CRI of 86. Even at 10000 and 15000 cd m high PEs (45.8 and 38.5 Im W and EQEs (24.3 and 22.1%) are maintained. Lighting sources are generally characterized by their total emitted light, which is a factor of 1.7-2.3 times more than the forward viewing efficiencies [Ia] Therefore, the present device should have total PE and EQE values approaching 100 Im W and 50%, respectively, at 5000 cd m which are also the highest   levels   reported for WOLEDs with extra out-coupling  andlor multi-layer tandem structures, [14] as well as comparable to the most efficient lighting technologies [15] W-1","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":584.2533162434895,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":68.66666666666667,"r":527.0,"t":770.5866495768229},"charspan":[0,633],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"~2 56.5 Im and 26.3%, respectively, with CRI of 86. Even at 10000 and 15000 cd m high PEs (45.8 and 38.5 Im W and EQEs (24.3 and 22.1%) are maintained. Lighting sources are generally characterized by their total emitted light, which is a factor of 1.7-2.3 times more than the forward viewing efficiencies [Ia] Therefore, the present device should have total PE and EQE values approaching 100 Im W and 50%, respectively, at 5000 cd m which are also the highest   levels   reported for WOLEDs with extra out-coupling  andlor multi-layer tandem structures, [14] as well as comparable to the most efficient lighting technologies [15] W-1"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Table L. Summary of EL_performance for Devices 1, 2, 3 and 4.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":530.9199829101562,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":69.66666666666667,"r":379.6666666666667,"t":545.586649576823},"charspan":[0,61],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"Table L. Summary of EL_performance for Devices 1, 2, 3 and 4."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"footnote","orig":"Applied voltage required to reach a luminance of 1 cd m Values at 1000, 5000 and 10000 cd m respectively.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":396.25331624348956,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":70.33333333333333,"r":500.3333333333333,"t":425.91998291015625},"charspan":[0,105],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/5","text":"Applied voltage required to reach a luminance of 1 cd m Values at 1000, 5000 and 10000 cd m respectively."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"To elucidate the origin of the high performance of the Device 1, three reference devices Devices 2, 3 and 4) with the same configuration as Device 1 were fabricated by using double neat films of FPPCA (20 nm)Bepp2 (10 nm) and a single doping film of Beppz:FPPCA (D (1.5 wt%, 30 nm) and FPPCA (H):BZQPG (0.8 wt%, 30 nm) as the EML, respectively (see Figure S2 in ESI file) The efficiency-luminance (PE/EQE-L) characteristics of Devices 2, 3 and 4 and their EL spectra at different luminances (1000, 2500 and 5000 cd m are shown in Figures 3c and 4. The two emission in Device 2 are assigned to: (i) direct exciton generation on the and FPPCA molecules in the respective EML and (ii) singletltriplet excited state energy in the blue EML transferring to the green EML; these are similar to those of Device 1 (Figure 3b) where   both low-content dopants have  almost no effect on the inherent properties of the host of and FPPCA. Devices 3 and 4 comprise EMLs with peaks Beppz Beppz","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":88.9531391024343,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":68.66666666666667,"r":527.0,"t":385.58664957682294},"charspan":[0,978],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/6","text":"To elucidate the origin of the high performance of the Device 1, three reference devices Devices 2, 3 and 4) with the same configuration as Device 1 were fabricated by using double neat films of FPPCA (20 nm)Bepp2 (10 nm) and a single doping film of Beppz:FPPCA (D (1.5 wt%, 30 nm) and FPPCA (H):BZQPG (0.8 wt%, 30 nm) as the EML, respectively (see Figure S2 in ESI file) The efficiency-luminance (PE/EQE-L) characteristics of Devices 2, 3 and 4 and their EL spectra at different luminances (1000, 2500 and 5000 cd m are shown in Figures 3c and 4. The two emission in Device 2 are assigned to: (i) direct exciton generation on the and FPPCA molecules in the respective EML and (ii) singletltriplet excited state energy in the blue EML transferring to the green EML; these are similar to those of Device 1 (Figure 3b) where   both low-content dopants have  almost no effect on the inherent properties of the host of and FPPCA. Devices 3 and 4 comprise EMLs with peaks Beppz Beppz"}],"version":"1.10.0"}